From 7b9f2606cc2aec9e3237b19eb641fd6e7026e6e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:33:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui-gateway): every interrupt producer records why it
 stopped a model wait [daveey]

A turn cut short while waiting for the model saved the same bare
"Operation interrupted: waiting for model response (N s elapsed)." row whether the
user pressed Stop, the backend exited, the WS-orphan reaper fired or a lease takeover
won, and Stop logged nothing at normal level. The coach therefore filed every
"interrupted, then resume" as an agent fault and nobody could tell a slow first token
from a lost turn (self-heal agent-38bad5aced).

- _interrupt_session_turn takes a fixed reason (user_stop default, ws_orphan for the
  orphan reaper, backend_exit from _stop_turns_before_exit, lease_takeover,
  session_close); a non-user reason reaches agent.interrupt as its tool_reason and
  rides the compute-host interrupt frame to the isolated child.
- handle_api_interrupt / the budget-summary interrupt call record_api_interrupt:
  {reason, waited_s, prompt_tokens} on display_metadata.interrupt of the interrupted
  row (partial text, hidden placeholder or the closing sentinel row), result["interrupt"],
  and one INFO line "turn interrupted: reason=... waited=...s prompt_tokens=...".
  Visible text is unchanged.

Tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_interrupt_reason.py drives a real AIAgent through a fake
slow provider and interrupts it via session.interrupt, _stop_turns_before_exit, the
WS-orphan path and a lease takeover; each row carries its own reason (red before).
